  "title": "Can STM32N6 NPU be used directly from HAL without X-CUBE-AI?",
  "content": "<p>Hi ST Community,</p><p>I am working with an STM32N657 and would like to use the integrated NPU directly from my own C/C++ application.</p><p>I understand that X-CUBE-AI together with the Neural-ART can generate the code required to execute a neural-network model on the STM32N6 NPU.</p><p>However, I would like to understand whether it is possible to use the NPU without X-CUBE-A<strong>I</strong>.</p><p>Does STM32CubeIde provide HAL APIs that allow an application to directly initialize, configure, load, and start the STM32N6 NPU?</p>",
